---
/* Strive AI, told as my part in it rather than as the product: a short deck of
   numbered "slides", each a headline, two or three pointers and a drawing. The
   technical teardown lives in /writing/generative-ui-chat-engine/, linked from
   the big card at the end. */
import WorkLayout from '../../layouts/WorkLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import StriveChat from '../../components/sketches/StriveChat.astro';
import RoleLoop from '../../components/sketches/strive/RoleLoop.astro';
import FoundationStack from '../../components/sketches/strive/FoundationStack.astro';
import BuildVsOwn from '../../components/sketches/strive/BuildVsOwn.astro';
import CanvasBeforeAfter from '../../components/sketches/strive/CanvasBeforeAfter.astro';
import AiElements from '../../components/sketches/strive/AiElements.astro';
import ParserContracts from '../../components/sketches/strive/ParserContracts.astro';
import SketchLive from '../../components/SketchLive.astro';

const description = "Strive AI, a chat that answers in live interfaces, and my part in building it with a small team: the foundations, the bet on owning the chat, moving the canvas beside the thread, and the AI elements, parser and contracts underneath.";

const lessons = [
  { miss: 'Rendered rich slots inline, in the thread.', lesson: 'Give big surfaces their own room. The container should fit the content, not the other way round.' },
  { miss: 'Asked the model for one giant JSON per answer.', href: '/writing/generative-ui-chat-engine/#where-it-started-to-hurt', lesson: 'Make complexity additive. One bad block should never sink the whole reply.' },
  { miss: 'Worried a side panel would look like a copy.', lesson: 'Familiar is a feature. Stand out on what goes inside the pattern.' },
  { miss: 'No AI playbook on the team, me included.', lesson: 'Benchmark, borrow, break, repeat. Ship small and learn in production.' },
];
---
<WorkLayout
  title="Strive AI — generative UI chat"
  description={description}
  ogDescription="Strive AI, a chat that answers in live interfaces, and my part in building it with a small team."
  eyebrow="Strivelabs · Design engineer · 2024 → now"
  heading="Strive AI"
  facts={[
    { label: 'Role', value: 'Design engineer · frontend' },
    { label: 'Team', value: '5–6 engineers · CTO + I built the foundation, the team built on it' },
    { label: 'Status', value: 'In production, still shipping' },
  ]}
  link={{ href: 'https://strivelabs.ai/', label: 'strivelabs.ai' }}
  schema={{
    name: 'Strive AI — generative UI chat',
    url: 'https://strivelabs.ai/',
    description: 'The chat surface Strive agents reach the user through: a from-scratch streaming engine, a block and slot vocabulary, and rich generative interfaces rendered live.',
    inLanguage: 'en',
    keywords: 'generative UI, AI chat, design engineering, UX for AI, design systems, AI elements, streaming, React, TypeScript',
  }}
>
  <StriveChat slot="sketch" />

  <Fragment slot="lede">A marketing chat that answers in <mark class="hl">live interfaces, not paragraphs</mark>, and today the way customers get almost everything done in Strive. This is my side of the story.</Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="glance">
    <div class="at-glance-row">
      <h3>The problem</h3>
      <p>We wanted one way to get things done in Strive, and chat was becoming the front door to work in the AI era. So we set out to power the whole platform through chat. </p>
    </div>
    <div class="at-glance-row">
      <h3>My part</h3>
      <div>
        <ul class="doodle-list">
          <li><strong>Research and the bet.</strong> Learnt how the frontier labs, like Anthropic and OpenAI, approach generative UI, and weighed potential ready-to-use fits such as the Vercel AI SDK and Thesys. Then <a href="/writing/generative-ui-chat-engine/#a-little-bit-of-backstory">made the case for owning the base</a>.</li>
          <li><strong>The chat, with our CTO.</strong> The two of us built it from the ground up: UI contracts, progressive streaming, retries and failures, and chat UX designed in code.</li>
          <li><strong>Foundations first.</strong> The design system, component registry and AI elements, with Storybook and documented contracts, were in place before any wiring.</li>
          <li><strong>Slot types.</strong> On our CTO’s slot foundation, I designed the slot types and shared one agent UI between chat and the standalone app.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Our CTO owned the backend, infra and the idea of slots. The wider team added to the base as it grew.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="at-glance-row">
      <h3>Shipped</h3>
      <p>In production with customers. It’s the core of Strive today: almost everything happens through chat.</p>
    </div>
  </Fragment>

  <div class="story">
    <section class="slide" aria-labelledby="s-role">
      <header class="slide-head">
        <span class="slide-num" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
        <div><p class="slide-kicker">How I work</p><h2 id="s-role">Build it so everyone can build</h2></div>
      </header>
      <ul class="doodle-list slide-points">
        <li><strong>Design in code.</strong> I designed the chat UX straight in code, and built every component standalone in Storybook, so each one is easy to build and test on its own.</li>
        <li><strong>Docs as context, for people and agents.</strong> As the team’s core frontend engineer, I set up the foundations so everyone could build interfaces with AI coding agents. The docs are their context, so I’ve kept them up to date with every version since.</li>
      </ul>
      <SketchLive id="storybook" live={{ kind: 'image', src: '/images/work/strive-ai/storybook.webp', width: 1800, height: 935, alt: 'Our Storybook: the component list on the left, and the docs page for TabbedChart showing a chart with reference lines, areas and dots, with a Show code button.' }} caption="The real thing: a chart in our Storybook, built and documented on its own.">
        <RoleLoop />
      </SketchLive>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" aria-labelledby="s-found">
      <header class="slide-head">
        <span class="slide-num" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
        <div><p class="slide-kicker">Foundations</p><h2 id="s-found">Bones before features</h2></div>
      </header>
      <ul class="doodle-list slide-points">
        <li>Defined <strong>primitives, AI elements, screens and layouts</strong> before features piled on.</li>
        <li>Those layers became the base of our <strong>block</strong> concept: everything the model renders is built from them.</li>
      </ul>
      <FoundationStack />
    </section>

    <section class="slide" aria-labelledby="s-bet">
      <header class="slide-head">
        <span class="slide-num" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
        <div><p class="slide-kicker">The bet</p><h2 id="s-bet">Own the chat, don't rent it</h2></div>
      </header>
      <ul class="doodle-list slide-points">
        <li>Streaming and AI elements: <strong>build it ourselves, or pull in a ready-made kit?</strong></li>
        <li>I bet on owning it. Chat is the core, and flexible interfaces are our moat.</li>
      </ul>
      <BuildVsOwn />
      <p class="more-note"><a href="/writing/generative-ui-chat-engine/#a-little-bit-of-backstory">There’s a lot more behind this call: what we tried, what we weighed, and why. The full story is in the <span class="nowrap">blog<Icon name="arrow-right" /></span></a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" aria-labelledby="s-canvas">
      <header class="slide-head">
        <span class="slide-num" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
        <div><p class="slide-kicker">Design call · slots &amp; canvas</p><h2 id="s-canvas">Move the canvas out of the thread</h2></div>
      </header>
      <ul class="doodle-list slide-points">
        <li>Answers can be <strong>rich surfaces</strong>: artifacts, an editor, whole pre-built agent interfaces.</li>
        <li>We first rendered them inline. It worked, but it kept hurting my taste, so I redesigned slots to <strong>open in a right-hand panel</strong>.</li>
      </ul>
      <SketchLive id="slots" live={{ kind: 'image', src: '/images/work/strive-ai/slot-panel.webp', width: 1800, height: 1069, alt: 'Strive AI in use: the chat on the left starts the blog refresh agent, and its full interface opens in the right-hand panel, a table of blog posts with their keywords, status and review actions.' }} caption="The real thing: the blog refresh agent’s full interface, open beside the thread.">
        <CanvasBeforeAfter />
      </SketchLive>
      <aside class="qa sk-box sk-lean-2" aria-label="The debate">
        <div class="qa-row qa-row--team">
          <span class="qa-av qa-av--team" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
          <p class="qa-bubble qa-q"><span>Team</span>"Isn't that just a Claude copy?"</p>
        </div>
        <div class="qa-row qa-row--me">
          <p class="qa-bubble qa-a"><span>Me</span>Claude set the standard, and this fixes our usability problems. If it's the right way to present, we use it and make what goes inside the panel ours.</p>
          <img class="qa-av qa-av--me" src="/images/portraits/me.webp" alt="" width="80" height="80" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        </div>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" aria-labelledby="s-elements">
      <header class="slide-head">
        <span class="slide-num" aria-hidden="true">05</span>
        <div><p class="slide-kicker">AI elements registry</p><h2 id="s-elements">The pieces our use cases asked for</h2></div>
      </header>
      <ul class="doodle-list slide-points">
        <li><code>@strivelabs/ui-core</code> for the foundations, <code>@strivelabs/ui-blocks</code> for reusable blocks, with our AI elements across both.</li>
        <li>Most AI kits don’t ship with these. I thought a few less common pieces would suit marketers well, so I pitched them to the team as experiments, and designed and built the ones that stuck. Five I’d pin:</li>
      </ul>
      <SketchLive id="elements" live={{ kind: 'video', src: '/images/work/strive-ai/ai-elements-charts.mp4', poster: '/images/work/strive-ai/ai-elements-charts-poster.webp', width: 1600, height: 950, alt: 'Screen recording of Strive AI: an impressions and spend chart with a launch line, a spend target, a peak dot and a shaded promo period, with series toggled from the legend; then an editable keyword list grouped by match type, with edit and delete on each row.' }} caption="The real thing: two of the five, a chart with markers and the editable list, in a live chat.">
        <AiElements />
      </SketchLive>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" aria-labelledby="s-under">
      <header class="slide-head">
        <span class="slide-num" aria-hidden="true">06</span>
        <div><p class="slide-kicker">Under the UI</p><h2 id="s-under">A parser and a contract for everything</h2></div>
      </header>
      <ul class="doodle-list slide-points">
        <li><strong>Custom streaming parser</strong> between backend blocks and the renderer. Inspired by <a href="https://github.com/globalaiplatform/langdiff" rel="noopener">langdiff</a>, extended with our platform specifics.</li>
        <li><strong>One contract system</strong> for interactive, read-only and stateful components alike. Hard to get right, and it took a lot of client and server pairing.</li>
      </ul>
      <ParserContracts />
    </section>

    <section class="slide" aria-labelledby="s-lessons">
      <header class="slide-head">
        <span class="slide-num" aria-hidden="true">07</span>
        <div><p class="slide-kicker">Misses &amp; lessons</p><h2 id="s-lessons">What I'd tell day-zero me</h2></div>
      </header>
      <ul class="lessons">
        {lessons.map((l, i) => (
          <li class:list={['sk-box', `sk-lean-${i + 1}`]}>
            <p class="lessons-miss"><span>Miss</span>{l.href ? <a href={l.href}>{l.miss}</a> : l.miss}</p>
            <p class="lessons-learn"><span>Lesson</span>{l.lesson}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </section>

    <a class="deep-dive wobbly wobbly--2" href="/writing/generative-ui-chat-engine/">
      <span class="deep-dive-shot taped ink-shot">
        <img src="/images/writing/generative-ui-chat-engine/sketch-chat-engine.png" alt="" width="2400" height="1419" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
      </span>
      <span class="deep-dive-body">
        <span class="deep-dive-eyebrow"><Icon name="pen" />Deep dive · ~15 min read</span>
        <strong>From answers to UI: how we built Strive’s generative UI engine</strong>
        <span class="deep-dive-sub">The options we weighed, why we took the bet, and everything that broke along the way.</span>
        <span class="deep-dive-go">Read the full story<Icon name="arrow-right" /></span>
      </span>
    </a>
  </div>
</WorkLayout>

<style>
  /* The story runs the full width of the narrow wrap; only the pointers keep a
     reading measure. */
  :global(.prose:has(> .story)) { max-width: none; }
  .story :global(.sk-fig) { margin: var(--space-3) 0 0; }

  .slide { margin-top: var(--space-5); padding-top: var(--space-3); border-top: 1.5px dashed var(--line); }
  .slide-head { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .slide-num { flex: none; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 6vw, 3.8rem); line-height: .85; color: var(--coral); }
  .slide:nth-of-type(2n) .slide-num { color: var(--blue); }
  .slide:nth-of-type(3n) .slide-num { color: var(--teal); }
  .slide-kicker { margin: 0 0 .3rem !important; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .7rem; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-faint); }
  .prose .slide-head h2 { margin: 0; }
  .slide-points { max-width: 60ch; }
  .slide-points li { font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.55; }
  .slide-points strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 500; }

  /* A handwritten pointer from a slide to the long-form post. */
  .more-note { margin: 1rem 0 0 !important; max-width: none; text-align: right; }
  .more-note a { font-family: var(--font-hand); font-size: 1.2rem; line-height: 1.25; color: var(--coral); text-decoration: none; }
  .more-note .nowrap { white-space: nowrap; }
  .more-note a:hover { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .more-note :global(.doodle) { width: 1.1rem; height: 1.1rem; margin-left: .3rem; vertical-align: -.15em; transition: transform .2s ease; }
  .more-note a:hover :global(.doodle) { transform: translateX(3px); }

  /* The "Claude copy?" exchange, as two chat lines. */
  /* A handwritten pointer from a slide to the long-form post. */
  .more-note { margin: 1rem 0 0 !important; max-width: none; text-align: right; }
  .more-note a { font-family: var(--font-hand); font-size: 1.2rem; line-height: 1.25; color: var(--coral); text-decoration: none; }
  .more-note a:hover { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .more-note :global(.doodle) { width: 1.1rem; height: 1.1rem; margin-left: .3rem; vertical-align: -.15em; transition: transform .2s ease; }
  .more-note a:hover :global(.doodle) { transform: translateX(3px); }

  /* The "Claude copy?" exchange, as a two-line chat: the team on the left with a
     huddle of faces, me on the right with my portrait. */
  .qa { margin-top: var(--space-3); padding: 1.1rem 1.1rem 1.2rem; display: grid; gap: .9rem; }
  .qa-row { display: flex; align-items: flex-end; gap: .65rem; }
  .qa-row--me { justify-content: flex-end; }
  .qa-bubble { margin: 0 !important; max-width: min(34rem, 100%); padding: .6rem .85rem .7rem; font-size: .95rem; line-height: 1.5; border: 1.5px solid var(--line); }
  .qa-bubble span { display: block; margin-bottom: .15rem; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .6rem; font-style: normal; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-faint); }
  .qa-q { color: var(--ink-soft) !important; font-style: italic; background: var(--sand); border-radius: 14px 14px 14px 4px; }
  .qa-a { color: var(--ink) !important; background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--teal) 10%, var(--paper-2)); border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--teal) 45%, transparent); border-radius: 14px 14px 4px 14px; }
  .qa-a span { color: var(--teal); }
  .qa-av { flex: none; width: 2.4rem; height: 2.4rem; border-radius: 50%; border: 1.5px solid var(--ink); }
  .qa-av--me { object-fit: cover; background: var(--sand); }
  /* Three small faces in a huddle: "the team", without naming anyone. */
  .qa-av--team { position: relative; background: var(--sand-2); overflow: hidden; }
  .qa-av--team i { position: absolute; bottom: -.35rem; width: 1.15rem; height: 1.5rem; border-radius: 50% 50% 40% 40%; border: 1.5px solid var(--ink); }
  .qa-av--team i:nth-child(1) { left: -.1rem; background: var(--coral-soft); }
  .qa-av--team i:nth-child(2) { right: -.1rem; background: var(--blue); opacity: .85; }
  .qa-av--team i:nth-child(3) { left: .55rem; bottom: -.2rem; background: var(--yellow); z-index: 1; }

  .lessons { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1.2rem; }
  .lessons li { display: grid; gap: .55rem; align-content: start; padding: .9rem 1rem 1rem; }
  .lessons p { margin: 0 !important; max-width: none; font-size: .9rem; line-height: 1.45; }
  .lessons span { display: block; margin-bottom: .1rem; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .62rem; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .lessons-miss { color: var(--ink-faint) !important; }
  .lessons-miss span { color: var(--coral); }
  .lessons-miss a { color: inherit; }
  .lessons-miss a:hover { color: var(--ink); }
  .lessons-learn { color: var(--ink) !important; font-weight: 500; }
  .lessons-learn span { color: var(--teal); font-weight: 400; }
  @media (max-width: 559px) { .lessons { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }

  /* The big card to the long-form write-up. */
  .deep-dive { display: block; margin-top: var(--space-5); padding: 1.2rem; text-decoration: none; color: var(--ink); box-shadow: 4px 5px 0 var(--shadow-ink); transition: transform .2s ease, box-shadow .2s ease; }
  .deep-dive:hover { color: var(--ink); transform: translateY(-3px); box-shadow: 6px 8px 0 var(--shadow-ink); }
  .deep-dive-shot { display: block; aspect-ratio: 16 / 7; overflow: visible; border: 1.5px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px 5px 12px 6px / 6px 12px 5px 10px; background: #fff; transform: rotate(-.6deg); transition: transform .25s ease; }
  .deep-dive:hover .deep-dive-shot { transform: rotate(0); }
  .deep-dive-shot img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; object-position: 0 30%; border-radius: inherit; }
  .deep-dive-body { display: grid; gap: .45rem; padding: 1.2rem .3rem .2rem; }
  .deep-dive-eyebrow { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .45rem; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .7rem; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-faint); }
  .deep-dive-eyebrow :global(.doodle) { color: var(--coral); width: 1.1rem; height: 1.1rem; }
  .deep-dive strong { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3.2vw, 2.1rem); font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -.02em; }
  .deep-dive-sub { font-size: 1rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .deep-dive-go { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: .35rem; margin-top: .3rem; font-weight: 500; color: var(--coral); }
  .deep-dive-go :global(.doodle) { width: 1rem; height: 1rem; stroke-width: 2; transition: transform .2s ease; }
  .deep-dive:hover .deep-dive-go :global(.doodle) { transform: translateX(4px); }
</style>
